@verbs get take drop give put
@tier player
@title moving things: from the floor to you, from you to somebody
@see wear consent inventory

  get <item> [from <something>]

Whatever is on the floor, or inside something you can open, comes
to your hands. Without the 'from', it is looked for where you are.

  drop <item>

Leaves it where you are. Not everything can be dropped: something
that is properly yours, such as the orb, refuses.

  give <item> to <somebody>
  put <item> in <something>

These are the same verb with two prepositions. Nobody receives
anything unwillingly: somebody whose 'dar' consent is not set to
yes tells you they will not take it, and learns that you tried.
